course: dictionary
lesson: 12920
title: Ethically: doing what is right and fair
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ethically is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something: in a way that is right and fair. Ethics is the word for thinking about what is right and wrong.
explain: «The team decided to act ethically, even when no one was watching.» Even when nobody can see you, the team still chooses what is right and fair. The clue is in the words around it: even when no one was watching shows that they could have cheated but did not.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The team decided to act in a right and fair way, even when no one was watching.» It still makes sense, so you have understood ethically.
fact: Ethically means in a way that is right and fair.
fact: «From a moral point of view» means thinking about what is right and wrong.
fact: «Ethically sourced» means made or grown in a fair way, so the workers were treated well.
fact: «Ethically tested» means tested in a careful and fair way.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «She chose chocolate that was ethically sourced.» What does ethically mean here? | Very loudly | In a hurry | In a cheap way, saving lots of money | *In a way that is right and fair
exercise: Ruby says, «Ethically, we should share the last biscuit.» What does ethically suggest? | *Thinking about what is fair and right | Thinking only about what you want | Feeling sleepy | Counting the biscuits quickly
exercise: «The team decided to act ethically, even when no one was watching.» Find and copy the word that means in a way that is right. | watching | *ethically | team | decided
test: «The shop only sells ethically made toys.» What does ethically mean in this sentence? | Without any money | In a bright or colourful way | *In a way that is right and fair | Very fast
test: What does «from a moral point of view» mean? | *Thinking about what is right and wrong | Looking at the colour of something | Counting the money that was spent | Looking at how fast something moves
exam: Which sentence uses ethically correctly? | *The company paid its workers fairly, acting ethically | The sun was ethically bright over the hills | He ran ethically fast to the bus | The cat slept ethically on the sofa
